This extension adds Middle-earth: Shadow of War modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]DLL and Packet Loaders automatically installed.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]

[list]
[*]❌ Xbox (Game Pass) is NOT supported due to folder permission restrictions.[/*]
[/list]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Packet Loader installs to the "x64\plugins" folder, recognised by a "ShadowOfWarPacketLoader.dll" file.[/*]
[*]DLL Loader installs to the "x64" folder, recognised by a "ShadowOfWarDllLoader.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Middle-Earth-Mod-Loader installs to the "x64" folder, recognised by a "bink2w64.dll" file and a "modloader" folder.[/*]
[*]Mods with a ".arch06" file install to the "Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugins / Packets mods with a ".dll" file, a "PacketLoader" folder and an "Internal" folder install to the "x64\plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "game" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "x64\plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatic install of DLL Loader and Packet Loader[/*]
[*].arch06 mods are installed to the "Mods" folder. Includes Load Order support and automatic default.archcfg update. Vortex will display a popup to select files if there's more than one .arch06 file in the mod archive.[/*]
[*]All other mods are installed to "x64/plugins" with a fallback notification.[/*]
[*][size=2]There is a button to download the legacy [url=https://github.com/ReaperAnon/Middle-Earth-Mod-Loader]Middle-Earth-Mod-Loader[/url]﻿, if you prefer to use that. Note that you can only have one DLL loader enabled at a time.[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Middle-earth: Shadow of War mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Packetloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ShadowOfWarPacketLoader.dll" file.

  Installs to: "x64\plugins"

========================================================================

Dllloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ShadowOfWarDllLoader.dll" file.

  Installs to: "x64"

========================================================================

Modloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "bink2w64.dll" file and a "modloader" folder.

  Installs to: "x64"

========================================================================

Arch06mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".arch06" file.

  Installs to: "Mods"

========================================================================

Pluginsandpackets:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" file, a "PacketLoader" folder and a "Internal" folder.

  Installs to: "x64\plugins"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── game\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "game" or "x64" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: "x64\plugins"

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

